# {{ name }} — service notes
- Generated by `make new-service`. Finish `REGISTER.md` (the guardrail snippets) before anything
  else: `make check` fails until it is done. Then delete `REGISTER.md`.
- Business rules: `application/use_cases/*` (process) and `application/policies/*` (math). The
  `R<n>` lists are the contract. `Ping` is a placeholder: delete it, its route and its test once
  the first real use case lands (`make new-use-case SVC={{ name }} NAME=<verb_noun>`).
- Local: `make up infra`, then `make up {{ name }}`; API at http://localhost:{{ api_port }}/docs
  and admin at http://localhost:{{ api_port }}/admin. Dev auth needs the `X-Tenant-Id` header.
- `{{ NAME }}_ENVIRONMENT` and `{{ NAME }}_AUTH_MODE` are required. Dev auth and the admin exist
  only in `local/dev/test/ci`. Prod uses `auth_mode=oidc`, which is not implemented yet
  (`backend_for` raises `NotImplementedError`), so prod fails closed until OIDC lands. Do not
  stub it, and never set dev auth in prod.
- Only the migrate process gets `{{ NAME }}_MIGRATOR_URL` (BYPASSRLS) and
  `{{ NAME }}_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL`; they are optional in `Settings`, and `{{ name }}.migrate`
  refuses to run without them. Every other process gets only the `sb_app` URL.
- Only the API mounts the admin, so only `{{ name }}-api` gets `{{ NAME }}_ADMIN_*`. They are
  optional in `Settings`; `build_api` calls `settings.admin_credentials()` outside prod before
  building anything, so a missing or short credential fails the API at startup.
- The admin's list views run as `sb_app` with no tenant set, so RLS shows them **zero rows**
  (Plan 4 ruling D9). Never point the admin at `migrator_url`.
- Run the API as `python -m {{ name }}.main` (uvicorn with `log_config=None`), never the bare
  `uvicorn` CLI, so uvicorn logs go through redaction. Never enable SQLAlchemy `echo`.
- Tests import the in-memory fakes as `from {{ name }}_fakes import ...`
  (`tests/{{ name }}_fakes.py`). `tests/conftest.py` puts `tests/` on `sys.path`. The module is
  named `<service>_fakes` (never plain `fakes`) because one pytest session shares `sys.modules`
  across services. The fakes stage writes until `commit()` and mirror `SqlAlchemyUnitOfWork`'s
  single-use lifecycle; use `fake_joined(outer)` where production passes `sb_db.uow.joined(uow)`.
  Add a fake repository for every repository port you add.
- DB tests run on their own `{{ name }}_test` database in the shared test Postgres. Request
  `{{ name }}_db` (sb_app URL), `{{ name }}_sessions` (the one session engine) or
  `{{ name }}_migrator_url`; never `postgres_url`, `postgres_app_url` or `postgres_migrator_url`
  directly. `tests/integration/db/test_migrations.py` downgrades that database to base and back,
  so every test creates its own tenant and never relies on rows from another test.
- Entity ids are server-generated (`sb_kernel.ids.new_id`), never taken from a client: primary
  keys are global, so a duplicate-id `Conflict` would reveal that an id exists in another tenant.
- Audit payloads carry no free-text PII (names, notes): the audit chain is append-only.
- The HTTP API contract is `contracts/openapi/{{ name }}.json`. Route function names are its
  operationIds. After changing a route or schema run `make openapi` and commit the diff.
- Messaging, workflows, acceptors and new tables: the `kafka-event`, `temporal-workflow`,
  `admin-acceptor` and `alembic-migration` skills.
